  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Web",
  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING - teardown now deletes a SQL row a finder located. Previously WebExt.ArtifactFinder.Sql produced observed references that teardown left in place; now the reference can address its row and the timeline decides whether it may be deleted. Chain MarkReadonly() onto the FindArtifact / FindArtifacts call for a row the run only reads. Requires TestFramework.Core 0.3.0 and TestFramework.Config 0.2.1.\nWhat to change: any timeline that locates existing rows - a row the application under test wrote, or a seeded fixture the suite shares - must add MarkReadonly() before upgrading. Without it, teardown deletes those rows. A row the test creates through SetupArtifact plus AddArtifact is unaffected: it was deleted before and still is.\nThe SqlRowArtifactReference public constructor no longer takes ownership into account; ownership is expressed on the timeline step instead of on the reference.",
